WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.884
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online English for Academic Purposes.

2
00:00:06.184 --> 00:00:09.629
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.929 --> 00:00:16.041
Unit six: Understanding Lectures. Today you will follow the structure and main points of a lecture.

4
00:00:16.341 --> 00:00:18.958
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.226
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.083 --> 00:00:25.119
Introduce.

7
00:00:26.117 --> 00:00:28.302
Introduce means to present a topic.

8
00:00:28.917 --> 00:00:31.206
The lecturer introduces the topic.

9
00:00:31.817 --> 00:00:34.272
Your turn. Say: Introduce.

10
00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:38.134
Introduce.

11
00:00:38.883 --> 00:00:39.803
Digression.

12
00:00:40.817 --> 00:00:42.944
Digression means a side topic.

13
00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:45.259
That was a short digression.

14
00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:48.259
Your turn. Say: Digression.

15
00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:52.159
Digression.

16
00:00:52.917 --> 00:00:54.231
Emphasise.

17
00:00:55.217 --> 00:00:57.936
Emphasise means to give extra importance.

18
00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:00.608
She emphasises the key point.

19
00:01:01.217 --> 00:01:03.672
Your turn. Say: Emphasise.

20
00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:07.662
Emphasise.

21
00:01:08.417 --> 00:01:09.348
Recap.

22
00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:12.930
Recap means a short repeat of main points.

23
00:01:13.517 --> 00:01:15.272
The recap helps memory.

24
00:01:15.883 --> 00:01:18.733
Your turn. Say: Recap.

25
00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:22.475
Recap.

26
00:01:23.217 --> 00:01:24.264
Transition.

27
00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:27.633
Transition means a move to a new point.

28
00:01:28.217 --> 00:01:29.891
Listen for the transition.

29
00:01:30.483 --> 00:01:32.834
Your turn. Say: Transition.

30
00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:36.736
Transition.

31
00:01:37.483 --> 00:01:38.542
Illustrate.

32
00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:42.327
Illustrate means to explain with an example.

33
00:01:42.917 --> 00:01:44.580
He illustrates with a graph.

34
00:01:45.183 --> 00:01:47.696
Your turn. Say: Illustrate.

35
00:01:50.533 --> 00:01:51.581
Illustrate.

36
00:01:52.317 --> 00:01:53.364
Clarify.

37
00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:56.280
Clarify means to make clear.

38
00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:58.593
Please clarify that point.

39
00:01:59.183 --> 00:02:01.580
Your turn. Say: Clarify.

40
00:02:04.433 --> 00:02:05.643
Clarify.

41
00:02:06.383 --> 00:02:07.338
Reference.

42
00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:10.756
Reference means a mention of a source.

43
00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:12.804
Write down the reference.

44
00:02:13.417 --> 00:02:16.266
Your turn. Say: Reference.

45
00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:20.310
Reference.

46
00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:24.646
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.483 --> 00:02:28.179
Visal, how do I follow a fast lecture?

48
00:02:29.283 --> 00:02:38.379
Listen for the introduction, where the lecturer says what the talk will cover. Then listen for transitions such as moving on to or turning now to.

49
00:02:39.483 --> 00:02:41.135
How do I know what is important?

50
00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:51.555
Lecturers emphasise key points with phrases such as the key point is, remember that or this is important. They also repeat and slow down.

51
00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:54.487
What if I do not understand?

52
00:02:55.583 --> 00:03:04.958
Write a question mark in your notes and ask at the end or check the slides. You can also ask a classmate or your tutor to clarify.

53
00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:07.554
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:08.417 --> 00:03:11.368
Grammar focus: Signposting phrases.

55
00:03:11.668 --> 00:03:12.797
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:13.483 --> 00:03:15.715
Let me begin with the causes of the problem.

57
00:03:16.617 --> 00:03:18.848
To sum up, there are three main factors.

58
00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:26.409
Lecturers use signposts to show structure: let me begin with, moving on to, to illustrate this and to sum up.

59
00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:31.312
Be careful! Don't say: The lecturer emphasise the point.

60
00:03:33.267 --> 00:03:35.998
Say: The lecturer emphasises the point.

61
00:03:36.298 --> 00:03:38.088
Add es after she or he.

62
00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:41.483
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:43.721
A Clear Lecture.

64
00:03:44.021 --> 00:03:47.135
Professor Sok introduces the topic of urban growth.

65
00:03:48.133 --> 00:03:50.737
She says that she will cover three main points.

66
00:03:51.733 --> 00:03:54.905
After the first point she moves on with a clear transition.

67
00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:58.735
She emphasises that planning is the key factor.

68
00:03:59.733 --> 00:04:01.710
At the end she gives a short recap.

69
00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:07.313
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:10.753
An introduction says what the talk will blank.

71
00:04:11.053 --> 00:04:14.184
A, cover. B, hide. C, delete.

72
00:04:17.733 --> 00:04:19.640
The answer is A: cover.

73
00:04:20.783 --> 00:04:22.400
Moving on to is a blank.

74
00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:26.318
A, gap. B, transition. C, title.

75
00:04:29.867 --> 00:04:32.110
The answer is B: transition.

76
00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:35.087
A recap is a short blank.

77
00:04:35.387 --> 00:04:38.506
A, joke. B, map. C, repeat.

78
00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:44.147
The answer is C: repeat.

79
00:04:45.283 --> 00:04:47.306
To clarify means to make blank.

80
00:04:47.606 --> 00:04:50.586
A, clear. B, loud. C, late.

81
00:04:54.133 --> 00:04:55.634
The answer is A: clear.

82
00:04:56.783 --> 00:04:59.015
What does Professor Sok emphasise?

83
00:04:59.315 --> 00:05:02.678
A, sport. B, planning. C, weather.

84
00:05:06.233 --> 00:05:08.175
The answer is B: planning.

85
00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:12.611
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:15.043
How do you follow a lecture?

87
00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:25.281
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:25.581 --> 00:05:37.663
I listen for the introduction and the transitions. I notice phrases that emphasise the key points. If I do not understand, I mark my notes and ask a question afterwards.

89
00:05:37.963 --> 00:05:39.812
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:40.717 --> 00:05:45.215
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and signposting phrases.

91
00:05:45.515 --> 00:05:49.247
Today's value is attention. Look carefully and listen well.

92
00:05:49.547 --> 00:05:51.828
See you in Unit seven. Goodbye!

93
00:05:52.128 --> 00:05:54.676
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

